 \paragraph{Acquisition variants.} We evaluated five uncertainty-driven acquisitions in addition to the primary greedy policy. These span the standard taxonomy of myopic acquisition functions~\citep{shahriari2015taking}. Improvement-based policies were EI~\citep{jones1998efficient} and probability of improvement~\citep{kushner1964new}. The optimistic policy was the GP lower confidence bound~\citep{srinivas2012information}, with $\beta=2$. Information-theoretic max-value entropy search~\citep{wang2017max} used a Gumbel approximation and ten max-value samples. Thompson sampling~\citep{russo2018tutorial} provided the sampling-based policy. Each replaced only the LF acquisition, leaving the surrogate, round-robin schedule, HF step and seeds fixed. Acquisition used the HF predictive mean, BLR standard deviation and HF incumbent (Supplementary Note~\ref{suppnote:blr}). All five TL surrogates ran on nine benchmarks with $5\times 9\times 20$ seeds per acquisition, using seeds 42--61.
 
