 \paragraph{HF-only controls.} Supplementary Table~\ref{supptab:hf_only_baselines} compares the multi-fidelity surrogates of Fig.~\ref{fig:final_regret} with two HF-only controls. The single-fidelity GP (SFGP) uses EI, and Random HF samples uniformly (definitions in the table footnotes). Both start from the same two initial HF points and spend the whole budget on HF evaluations. Attainment is computed over each arm's own window. The HF-only arms are therefore scored from the end of their initial design, at 2 HF-equivalent units.
 
